tial vision, connections), decision quality unknown, attention unknown, crew cooperation unknown, communication unknown, responsibility unknown, adaptability low (not open to new ideas).\n\nGiven B's strong reliability and stress but communication issues, C's strong decision and crew cooperation but communication difficulty, D's responsibility and problem solving but temper, A's anticipation but show-off.\n\nWhich candidate best overall? Probably C because crew cooperation positive, calm under pressure, decision quality, technical competence, though communication difficulty. But communication is important. B's communication is pretentious and nasty remarks, which could be more severe. C's difficulty communicating ideas may be less severe than nasty remarks. Also C's egocentric may affect crew but positive atmosphere suggests good cooperation.\n\nThus I might shift recommendation to Candidate C. Provide argument referencing evidence: C keeps calm in crisis, makes correct decisions quickly, creates positive atmosphere, but has communication difficulty. Compare to B's pretentiousness and nasty remarks which could harm crew safety more. Also B's weak memory for numbers is a safety risk. So C seems better overall.\n\nThus I will state my vote for Candidate C, explaining why.\n\nPublic message: reference Agent 3's recommendation of B, Agent 1's concerns, and new info from Agent 1 about C's crew cooperation positive, D unknown. Argue that C's strengths in stress resilience, decision quality, crew cooperation outweigh communication difficulty, and B's communication and memory issues are more concerning.\n\nProceed."}
